 "readme_lines_removed": [
  "Every number below is read from `ecbench compare` or `ecbench band` output, or from the card's `phase_sums.json`, in `P<b>/{wall,counted}/analysis/`. Nothing here is computed by hand.",
  "**Not relabelling, not accounting.** dg and dgb charge identical work record by record at every size, so their counted S is identical (see the next table). The wall difference is executed native work: a different memory layout for the same table.",
  "The blocked build roughly halves the oracle set-up, but probing the packed table in the target PDP phase is slower than probing FastMap (+5%, +34% and +21%). The probe cost gives back part of the set-up gain, which is why every ratio missed its prediction. E6 flagged this risk, and PR #2844's table-floor micro-benchmark points the same way: a flat one-region table is 2.3\u20132.9\u00d7 slower on misses."
 ],
